{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZjJUaEG1Fw2BEY7JUXN5n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nI found search results related to CoRL 2026, though specific detailed reviewer guidelines and review form information for 2026 are not fully available in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information Found:\n\n**Review Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Historical Guidelines:\n\nFor more comprehensive reviewer guidelines, the search found ICML and NeurIPS provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews, and CoRL's guidelines build on these resources.\n\nFrom CoRL 2023/2024 guidance, reviewers are expected to evaluate papers on criteria such as relevance to robot learning and the quality of limitations sections.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org or checking OpenReview at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference, as the specific review form details may not yet be publicly available or may be hosted on those platforms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cecc2908-68ca-4714-bd9d-0379a2878afb","uuid":"f7c83a2c-0df6-49f0-9af3-d443eba56f44","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:36:12.234Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Jmjezvm84TUdtWURMyRhAQ","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"I found search results related to CoRL 2026, though specific detailed reviewer guidelines and review form information for 2026 are not fully available in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information Found:\n\n**Review Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Historical Guidelines:\n\nFor more comprehensive reviewer guidelines, the search found ICML and NeurIPS provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews, and CoRL's guidelines build on these resources.\n\nFrom CoRL 2023/2024 guidance, reviewers are expected to evaluate papers on criteria such as relevance to robot learning and the quality of limitations sections.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org or checking OpenReview at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference, as the specific review form details may not yet be publicly available or may be hosted on those platforms."],"durationSeconds":6.14902259}}
